     2026 State Election Information 


 Only upcoming election information will be shown on this page. To view recent election results, see the  Election Results page . 
 Date 
 The State Election will be held Tuesday, November 3, 2026. 
 Warrant 
 An election warrant is an official, legal public notice and warning issued by the Selectboard that formally announces an upcoming election, details the polling hours and locations, and lists the offices or ballot questions to be voted on. 
 An online copy of the warrant will be posted here once signed by the Selectboard and posted by the Constable. 
 Information on the Ballot 

 The ballot will be multiple pages (cards) and double sided.  
 The Secretary of the Commonwealth’s Office has mailed printed copies of the 2026 Information for Voters Guide, affectionally known as the “Red Book”, to all households in September. You can review the online version of the  Information for Voters Guide  to stay informed of the offices and the 9 questions on the ballot prior to casting your vote. 

 Sample Ballot 
 You can view the sample ballot at the  Secretary of State’s page . 
 Ways to vote 
 Vote By Mail 

 Available upon request. 
 In September, all registered voters who have not requested a mail-in ballot for the State Election, will receive a postage pre-paid vote by mail application from the Secretary of State. 
 Mail-in ballots may also be requested online at the Secretary of State’s  Voting By Mail page . 
 The deadline to request a mail-in ballot for the State Election is 5:00 PM, Tuesday, October 27, 2026. 

 Vote Early In-Person 
 Early Voting In-Person will take place at Town Hall, 6 Town Hall Drive, Princeton, MA 01541. 
 Early Voting In-Person Hours for the State Election 

 Saturday, October 17, 2026, 8:00AM to 12:00PM 
 Monday, October 19, 2026, 9:00AM to 12:00PM 
 Tuesday, October 20, 2026, 9:00AM to 12:00PM 
 Wednesday, October 21, 2026, 12:00PM to 3:00PM 
 Thursday, October 22, 2026, 9:00AM to 12:00PM 
 Saturday, October 24, 2026, 9:30AM to 1:30PM 
 Monday, October 26, 2026, 9:00AM to 12:00PM 
 Tuesday, October 27, 2026, 9:00AM to 12:00PM 
 Wednesday, October 28, 2026, 12:00PM to 3:00PM 
 Thursday, October 29, 2026, 9:00AM to 12:00PM 

 Absentee Voting 
 Check the  Secretary of State’s webpage on Absentee Voting  to see if you are qualified to vote absentee by mail or in person and the application deadlines. 
 Election Day Voting 

 Available in all elections. 
 Polls will be open for state elections from 7:00 AM to 8:00 PM. 
 For local elections, polls will be open from 12:00 PM to 8:00 PM. 
 The polling location is Thomas Prince School Gymnasium located at 170 Sterling Rd, Princeton, MA 01541. 
 You can  check your voter registration online  and contact Clerk Horsung with questions at  [email protected]  or 978-464-2103. 









